[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]
\draw (0,0)--(7,0);
\foreach \x in {0,3.5,7} {\draw (\x,-0.12)--(\x,0.12);}
\node[below] at (0,-0.15) {$0$};
\node[below] at (3.5,-0.15) {$\frac{1}{2}$};
\node[below] at (7,-0.15) {$1$};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (0,-1.2) {Impossible};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (3.5,-1.2) {Even chance};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (7,-1.2) {Certain};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (1.75,0.4) {Unlikely};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (5.25,0.4) {Likely};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Using the probability scale, describe each event as impossible, unlikely, even chance, likely or certain.
a. The sun rises tomorrow morning.
b. A person jumps over the moon.
c. Rolling an even number on a standard six-sided die.
d. Winning the lottery.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]
\draw (0,0)--(7,0);
\foreach \x in {0,3.5,7} {\draw (\x,-0.12)--(\x,0.12);}
\node[below] at (0,-0.15) {$0$};
\node[below] at (3.5,-0.15) {$\frac{1}{2}$};
\node[below] at (7,-0.15) {$1$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,1.0)--(0,0.2);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (3.5,1.0)--(3.5,0.2);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (7,1.0)--(7,0.2);
\node at (0,1.3) {$A$};
\node at (3.5,1.3) {$B$};
\node at (7,1.3) {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Three probabilities are marked $A$, $B$ and $C$ on the scale. Match each event to the letter showing its probability.
a. A person jumps over the moon.
b. Rolling an even number on a standard six-sided die.
c. The sun rises tomorrow morning.

