\draw[-{Stealth}] (5.6,1.0)--(5.6,0.2);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (7,1.0)--(7,0.2);
\node at (0.7,1.3) {$A$};
\node at (3.5,1.3) {$B$};
\node at (5.6,1.3) {$C$};
\node at (7,1.3) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Four probabilities are marked $A$, $B$, $C$ and $D$ on the scale. Which arrow shows the probability of an event that is:
a. certain?
b. likely, but not certain?
c. unlikely, but not impossible?
